# Compact WPA/WPA2 wordlist-mutation rules for hashcat (-r).
# Curated for real Wi-Fi passwords, with a Philippine tilt:
# case, appended digits/years, leet, dup/reverse, PH mobile prefixes.
# Kept bounded so a full pass over a large wordlist stays practical on
# modest/integrated GPUs. Ref: hashcat rule_based_attack docs.
# c=Capitalize u=UPPER $x=append ^x=prepend sXY=substitute d=duplicate r=reverse

# Case variants
c
u
l

# Append single digits / years
$1
$2
$3
$4
$0
$7
$9
$!
$@
$12
$123
$1234
$2020
$2021
$2022
$2023
$2024
$2025

# Append common PH suffixes
$0917
$0918
$0919
$0920
$0921
$123!
$1234!
$2024!
$2023!

# Append double/triple digits
$00
$000
$11
$111
$22
$222
$99
$999

# Capitalize + append digit/year
c$1
c$12
c$123
c$2024
c$2023
c$0917
c$!
c$1$2$3

# Prepend digits (common for PH: 09 + name)
^0
^1
^2
^09
^091
^0917
^0918

# Prepend/append combos
^0$0
^1$1
^09$17
^09$18

# Repeated / patterned
$2$0$2$0
$2$0$2$1
$2$0$2$2
$2$0$2$3
$2$0$2$4
$2$0$2$5
$1$2$1$2
$1$2$3$4
$4$3$2$1

# Leet substitutions (PH passwords often use these)
sa@
se3
si1
so0
ss$
$5
$4
$3
$1
$0

# Leet + case + append
csa@cse3csi1cso0css$
cse3so0
csa@se3si1so0

# Duplicate / reverse / rotate
d
r
$d
$r

# PH nickname patterns: short name + year
$1$1
$2$2
$3$3
$7$7
$9$9

# Common PH sweet patterns
$123456
$1234567
$12345678
$password
$admin
$wifi
$internet
